<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 18.35 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 18.35 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	18.35	    + 65	    18.00     18.65</p>
<p>91-Day	19.18	    + 18	    19.00     19.23</p>
<p>181-Day     20.39	    + 14	    20.24     20.40</p>
<p>357-Day     20.52				20.48     20.56</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 20.24 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.20 bln pesos    2.75</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   3.30 bln pesos    4.13</p>
<p>181-Day     800 million pesos   3.04 bln pesos    3.80</p>
<p>357-Day     600 million pesos   2.57 bln pesos    4.29</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.70 on demand of 11.11 billion pesos compared to 3.44 the week before on demand of 10.31 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   30 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    5 basis points</p>
<p>    181-Day			   1 basis point</p>
<p>    357-Day			   4 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
